From 9aae4649e58cd993f756fe85d897d866dd990e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:25:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 096/141] fix(pypto-x): apply exp(A_log) in the GDR decay gate
 (graph contract v3)

The decoder graph computed the GDR decay gate as
``gate_log = -A_log * softplus(a + dt_bias)`` while the official model uses
``g = -exp(A_log) * softplus(a + dt_bias)``
(transformers/models/qwen3_5/modeling_qwen3_5.py: ``self.A_log =
nn.Parameter(torch.log(A))``).  Without ``exp`` the decay ``exp(g)`` exceeds
one for every head with a negative ``A_log`` (this checkpoint: A_log in
[-6.59, 0.26]), so the FP32 recurrent state grew exponentially (|state|max
0.60 -> 2.8e4 -> 2.36e16 over five prefill steps) and the whole-network logits
could not match the reference.

Effect on the real checkpoint (T=5 prefill, AVX-512): logits cosine 0.7771 ->
0.9999136, max_abs 17.99 -> 0.2338 (the reference's own fp32<->bf16 band is
0.2352), per-row argmax 1/5 -> 5/5.  Layer-0 GDR |state|max at step 4 becomes
1.43.  Decode steps 0..2 (positions 5..7) reproduce the gold argmax with
cosine >= 0.9998 once the driver compares our step k against
``decode_logits[k+1]`` (gold row 0 is the prefill boundary and is bit-identical
to ``prefill_next_logits``).

Chained effects recorded here and in the evidence brief:

* graph contract version 2 -> 3; decoder graph digest (past=4096) changes from
  c1a5663b... to 66dd4077...; decoder operation total 4,532 -> 4,550 (T=5:
  6,710 -> 6,728);
* the frozen digest in test_qwen35_weight_ingestion.py and the weight-ingestion
  driver PARENT_BASELINE are updated with an erratum comment, and
  test_qwen35_full_decoder_connectivity.py now expects contract version 3;
* previously frozen M1J artifacts (model-metadata.json in
  verify-qwen35-bf16-runtime-binding, integration-w6-qwen35-bf16-runtime-binding-final-r2,
  qwen35-bf16-weight-ingestion, parent-real-profile-probe) still carry the v2
  digest and need an erratum annotation; parameter bytes, packed layout regions
  and sizes are unchanged (371 params / 1,504,786,048 B / 368 regions);
* content-addressed native artifacts fail closed automatically because the
  native/program/plan digests all change;
* no lowering/artifact/ABI bump is required: only the portable graph changed.

M1G/M1D conclusions are unaffected: their drivers and composite builders take
``gate`` as a program input and validate ``S_decay = exp(g) * S``, which was
correct.  The gap was the construction of ``g`` from ``A_log`` in the full
decoder graph.

Also adds test_qwen35_gdr_decay_gate.py as a structural + semantic regression
guard for the fixed gate, and makes the driver's generate_logits cross-check
mask the EOS -inf position.
